  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "service",
      "title": "Shared runtime",
      "items": [
        "dmserver and embedded bench scenarios use server/internal/runtime. The runtime builds the application, opens the listener, and starts configured workers.",
        "TLS is optional for the listener; reverse-proxy deployments remain supported. Readiness is exposed for supervisors and acceptance checks."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "service",
      "title": "Role-specific services",
      "items": [
        "mdm and all expose device enrollment and /mdm. A remote declarative URL selects forwarding; ddm exposes the internal declarative adapter.",
        "Enrollment discovery and trust routes are mounted only when enrollment is configured. App push uses its own clients and credential store."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "neutral",
      "title": "Ordered shutdown",
      "items": [
        "Stop accepting requests and drain in-flight HTTP work, then stop and await workers. Close application resources and APNs clients afterward.",
        "The runtime preserves the first failure and bounds shutdown time."
      ]
    },
    {
